<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oral, Kazakhstan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Uralsk, Yaitsky Gorodok</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oral, known in Russian as Uralsk, is a city in north-western Kazakhstan on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ural-river">Ural River</a>. Founded in the early 17th century as Yaitsky Gorodok, the chief settlement of the Yaik <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossacks</a>, it was a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemelyan-pugachev">Yemelyan Pugachev</a>'s rebellion in 1773–1774, after which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-the-great">Catherine the Great</a> renamed the river and the town after the Urals. It is now the capital of West Kazakhstan Region.</p></div>
